 which was obviously  wrong or in 2019 when they claimed the  16-inch macbook pro would be coming in  september wrong again or even this year  when they claim the new macbook pros  with the m1x chips would be coming in  september and all signs are currently  pointing to them being wrong once again  so based on those failed leaks i don't  trust digitimes at all with this new one  about multiple events in september so  let's just place our bets on a single  event now as far as the event date  itself it's almost certainly going to be  on september 14th based on a new leak of  the pre-order dates for the iphone 13  which john prosser and leaks apple pro  have both confirmed already so we're  sticking to the 14th now moving on to  why the event is gonna blow you away  let's get into the first product that we  should expect and that's the iphone 13  lineup to get started i want to confirm  that it is going to be called the iphone  13 and not the 12s and that's based on a  new leak of apple packaging stickers  showing the iphone 13 name and to me  these look totally legit and this  actually adds on to another leak that  this year's phones will be called the  iphone 13 with the same four models as  we had last year which i totally agree  with but another point i want to make is  that in the past whenever apple had an s  version of an iphone it looked basically  identical to the original model for  example here's the back of the iphone 6  and the 6s spot the difference and right  here is the front  yep they're identical and here is the  iphone 10 on the left and the iphone 10s  on the right just kidding the 10 is  actually on the right and here's the  front the only difference we see are the  performance scores so if apple was to  call this year's iphone the iphone 12 s  we shouldn't be expecting any design  differences at all but that is wrong  completely wrong back in may mac rumors  claimed that the iphone 13 models would  be slightly thicker and would have  larger camera bumps with the biggest  difference being visible on the pro  models they also said that the camera  lens bumps themselves would be getting  thicker as well especially on the pro  models there was also a leaked case for  the 13 pro which showed an absolutely  massive camera bump difference which  signals a pretty big change  to the size of the camera lenses and  this goes hand in hand with a leak from  svet apple who shared a matching camera  bump size difference for the iphone 13  pro models as well as a smaller increase  for the regular 13s on top of that the  regular iphone 13 is rumored to have a  diagonal camera layout which means apple  is trying hard to make both the front  and the back look different compared to  the 12 signaling a new iphone 13 name  john prosser also claimed to have  received the actual cad files for the  iphone 13 models and those already  showed the new larger camera bumps on  the pro models and diagonal camera  layout on the regular 13s and then going  all the way back to january digitimes  actually claimed that apple would be  giving the iphone 13 a smaller notch and  the way they would do this is by  completely redesigning the face id  sensor system to pack more sensors into  one similar to how the lidar scanner  works on the rear and then a couple of  months later new images were released  showing the actual cover glass with the  redesigned notch being much smaller with  the biggest change being the speaker  grille moving to the top of the phone  right underneath the frame john prosser  recently confirmed the new face id  system in a video by showing off this  new device that apple is giving to their  employees which packs the new redesigned  sensor system which perfectly matches  the shorter notch sensor layout so apple  is essentially giving that device to  their employees instead of a legit  unreleased iphone 13 so that they can  test it to see if it'll work with masks  and foggy glasses without them risking  even more leaks going out and to make  all of this even better mark german a  very reliable analyst came out and  basically confirmed the smaller notch  rumor alongside other common leaks like  the pro models getting 120 hertz pro  motion displays and an a15 bionic chip  now i do want to mention that the 120  hertz rumor has been around for a very  long time and i think this is going to  be one of the major selling points for  the iphone 13 and what's great about it  is that the promotion tech could allow  the refresh rate to go as low as 1 hertz  which would be enough to enable an  always on display like apple already has  on the apple watch which german said is  a possibility for the iphone 13. but the  absolute biggest deal that mark german  confirmed was that the pro models will  be coming with a new portrait mode video  feature which would be called cinematic  video giving a nice blur to the  background in video recording in real  time that right there is going to be a  revolutionary feature that will make  everyone go crazy about the iphone 13  and in my opinion it's gonna work by  using a second generation lidar scanner  which will be exclusive to the pro  models so as you can tell there are  obviously enough external design changes  that apple can easily name it the iphone  13. especially since apple is expecting  to sell massive amounts of them based on  apple ordering over 100 million a15  chips as well as them outsourcing  production for more suppliers like  luxure and having foxconn hire an  additional 200 000 workers to keep up  with iphone 13 demand now before we get  into the crazy apple watch series 7  leaks and rumors let me just blast  through a bunch of other iphone 13 leaks  that i totally agree with the 13 pro  models are expected to get improved  ultra wide cameras with auto focus the  whole 13 lineup should be getting larger  wireless charging coils stronger max  safe magnets bigger batteries across the  board support for 25 watt fast charging  faster millimeter wave 5g speeds due to  apple using the new snapdragon x60 modem  wi-fi 6e support which uses the new 6  gigahertz band and much more now the  only issue is that there are rumors that  apple is increasing the price of the  iphone 13 because tsmc their main chip  supplier has just raised chip prices by  up to twenty percent for older chip  designs and three to ten percent for  their seven nanometer or smaller designs  which modern iphones use but in my  opinion i don't think that this will  impact the iphone 13 prices because  apple has already ordered all of those  chips before the price hike is happening  which is only supposed to go into effect  in january so the only reason that apple  would raise the prices on the iphone 13  lineup is if they want to do it early to  make up for some profits right now  before prices go up next year now with  the iphone finally out of the way let's  move on to the next big product and  that's the apple watch series 7. a  couple of months ago i thought that the  series 7 would be disappointing because  it may not be getting a redesign until  next year but recently we finally got  confirmation on august 17th 91 mobile's  released the cad files of the apple  watch series 7 showing off a full  redesign with flat sides which perfectly  matches up to john prosser's renders  that he showed us months ago on top of  that the cad files show off a redesigned  flat display panel and this leak matches  up to what mark german said recently  claiming that the new watch will have  thinner bezels and a flatter display  panel using a new lamination technique  to bring the display closer to the front  cover glass and this actually matches up  to a recent leak from weibo user uncle  pan claiming that the new series 7 will  come in larger 41 and 45 millimeter  sizes which will make the bezels thinner  like mark german already mentioned and  within the comments on that leak a weibo  user claimed that apple needs to make  the display perfectly flat  because they will be using ceramic  crystal glass like they're currently  already using in the iphone 12. and that  makes perfect sense and going even  further dan rue on twitter confirmed  that there will be a new 45 millimeter  display size by showing off a weibo leak  of a leather apple watch band with 45  millimeters printed on it which looks  legit and on top of that twitter user  majin buu showed us a leaked image of a  41 millimeter watch braided solo loop  watch band and a size of two and he says  that the bands have started mass  production so i did a little digging and  i compared that 41 millimeter text to  the text on a current braided solo loop  and it seemed to perfectly match up so i  think that leaked image of the 41  millimeter band is also totally legit  and finally just two days ago on sunday  mark german confirmed that there will in  fact be new 41 and 45 millimeter sizes  so i'm now basically 100 sure that the  series 7 will have a new redesign like  john prosser showed off in his renders  and this is gonna be a huge deal because  the exterior shape of the apple watch  has never changed before so this alone  is gonna cause a huge wave of upgrades  mark german also mentioned that we'll  have new watch faces to take advantage  of the larger displays including an  updated infographic modular face we'll  probably also see this world timer watch  face which was leaked back in june and  it looks amazing in my opinion and  beyond that we can also expect new  features like updated ultra wideband  technology and a faster s7 chip which  will be based on tsmc's five nanometer  process and a new double-sided packing  technology to save space and it might  even get an upgrade to 2 gigs of ram  there's also a chance that the display  will be using brand new micro led  technology which has been rumored for  years now but i honestly feel like that  would be giving us way too much in one  update so maybe apple is going to hold  off for another year on the micro led  display the series 7 is also rumored to  be getting a larger battery and a switch  to the more efficient wi-fi 6e and  potentially bluetooth 5.2 which will  give the watch much better battery life  and potentially allow apple to add 5g  connectivity this year but maybe not yet  and with that said this is probably  going to be the best time to buy an  apple watch basically ever especially if  you care about resale value and it's all  going to be due to the brand new design  now moving on to the next product on the  list we have the air pods 3 which are  expected to be revealed alongside the  iphone 13 at the september event and  this is big because everyone from dillon  dkt on twitter digitimes through a  report last month ming chi kuo from  multiple reports mark german from  various reports and supply chain details  like mass production of airpods 3  beginning and leaked launch dates  pointing to the airpods 3 releasing this  fall at the september event so it's  pretty much a sure thing at this point  now as far as the features we're not  really expecting much other than a new  design that looks similar to the airpods  pro but most likely without a sealed  design which means that they will not  have noise cancellation at all i  personally expect them to be priced  somewhere around a hundred and ninety  nine dollars putting them right between  apple's beat studio buds for 150 bucks  and the airpods pro for 250 dollars and  i also think that apple is going to be  selling a ton of them because there are  many people who are still using the  original airpods like myself or the  airpods 2 and they're probably looking  to upgrade soon alongside all the new  customers who will finally cave in and  buy airpods now moving on to the ipad  updates we're expecting both the ipad 9  and the ipad mini 6 to get revealed at  the event so let's start with the basic  ipad according to mark german it's going  to be a very small update with the main  difference being a thinner design which  will most likely come from apple finally  giving it a laminated display which will  improve the contrast colors and get rid  of that annoying gap between the display  and the cover glass on top of that mark  also mentioned that it will be getting a  more powerful processor which will  almost 100 percent be the a13 bionic  channel but other than that i'm  personally not expecting anything else  would the display probably sticking to  the same 10.2 inches with a possible  price bump up to 349 dollars but it  might just stick to the same 329 price  who knows and finally the ipad mini 6 is  expected to get a full redesign like the  renders that john prosser showed off a  couple of months back with apple giving  it the same design as the ipad air  including a touch id power button an  edge to edge display and magnetic apple  pencil wireless charging on the side and  in my opinion it's going to be sticking  to the same a14 bionic chip but there is  a chance that it's going to get upgraded  to the a15 and at this point i don't  think that it's going to get a mini led  display at least according to the  display analyst ross young and in terms  of the pricing it'll most likely cost  between 449 dollars and 499 dollars for  the base model with 64 gigs of storage  so there you guys have it those are all  the products that i'm expecting at  apple's september event here in just a  couple of weeks if you enjoyed this  video definitely click the circle above  to subscribe for more videos like this  one watch one of those two right over  there thanks for watching and we'll see  you in the next video  [Music]

